  "explanation": "For a nested bin the function recurses on that sublist twice (totalStock(first) + totalStock(first)), so the nested [2,3] group contributes 5 twice. The recursion still terminates, but the doubled group makes it print 14 instead of the correct 9.",
  "prompt": "This totals the stock in bins, recursing into any nested bin. Step through and predict the total it prints.",
  "language": "javascript",
  "snippet": "function totalStock(bins) {\n  if (bins.length === 0) return 0;\n  const first = bins[0];\n  if (Array.isArray(first)) {\n    return totalStock(first) + totalStock(first) + totalStock(bins.slice(1));\n  }\n  return first + totalStock(bins.slice(1));\n}\nconsole.log(totalStock([[2, 3], 4]));",
